      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(4,0)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=4f(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The function $y=4f(x)$ represents a stretch of the function $y=f(x)$ by a factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $4.$\n\nTherefore, the point $(4,0)$ on $f(x)$ is mapped to the point $(4,4\\cdot 0)=(4,0),$ and this point must lie on the graph of $y=4f(x).$",
